    {
      "html": "<p class=\"P1\">It shall be the duty of the city clerk to furnish, upon all proper occasions, such public records or papers as may be called for to the person who shall apply therefor and to place such records or papers in a convenient place in his office for examination.</p>\n<p class=\"HistoryNote\">(Rev. Ords. 1962, § 265)</p>\n<p class=\"Footnote\"><span class=\"bold\">Charter reference—</span>Furnishing certified copies of records, § <a class=\"basic\" href=\"/VT/Burlington/#!/BurlingtonCH/BurlingtonCH05.html#140\" rel=\"cgi/extract.pl?page=html/BurlingtonCH/BurlingtonCH05.html&amp;anchor=140\">140</a>.</p>",
      "text": "It shall be the duty of the city clerk to furnish, upon all proper occasions, such public records or papers as may be called for to the person who shall apply therefor and to place such records or papers in a convenient place in his office for examination. (Rev. Ords. 1962, § 265) Charter reference—Furnishing certified copies of records, § 140.",
