    {
      "html": "<p class=\"P1\">No book or volume of the public records or paper duly filed shall be taken from the office of the city clerk except on order of a court; provided, however, that upon giving a receipt therefor, the city attorney may take a paper on file which relates to the business of his office.</p>\n<p class=\"HistoryNote\">(Rev. Ords. 1962, § 263)</p>\n<p class=\"Footnote\"><span class=\"bold\">Charter reference—</span>Removal of records, § <a class=\"basic\" href=\"/VT/Burlington/#!/BurlingtonCH/BurlingtonCH05.html#139\" rel=\"cgi/extract.pl?page=html/BurlingtonCH/BurlingtonCH05.html&amp;anchor=139\">139</a>.</p>",
      "text": "No book or volume of the public records or paper duly filed shall be taken from the office of the city clerk except on order of a court; provided, however, that upon giving a receipt therefor, the city attorney may take a paper on file which relates to the business of his office. (Rev. Ords. 1962, § 263) Charter reference—Removal of records, § 139.",
